[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: The creator introduces the HeyGears G1X printer.
AUDIO: 'This is the HeyGears G1X, capable of full color 2D printing, 3D texture printing, and even full color 3D printing. Hello ladies and gentlemen, I\'m Dan, and welcome back to another printer review video. Today, I\'m joined by the HeyGears G1X desktop full color 3D and UV printer. Yeah, first try.'

[00:14] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: The creator talks about the HeyGears G1X, a desktop full color 3D and UV printer.
AUDIO: 'Before using this, my experience with UV printing was severely limited. I really only ever used the standard resin 3D printers. I previously reviewed the HeyGears Reflex RS Turbo resin 3D printer, and I got to say, I really'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'enjoyed using that machine. So much so that I actually still use that resin printer consistently to this day for anything that I have to resin print, which means I\'m extremely excited to see what this bad boy can do. I\'m going to quickly run over the specs for this UV'

[00:38] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: The creator discusses the specifications of the HeyGears G1X, including its Epson i3200 print head and 8-channel ink system.
AUDIO: 'printer. An Epson i3200 print head powers the G1X, and it uses an eight-channel ink system capable of producing over 10 million colors. It can print on more than 400 different base materials, features automatic'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'calibration, and can print both full color and transparent layers within the same print. But, before we get started, I do want to mention safety. Anytime you\'re going to be handling or dealing with resin, you want to make sure that you\'re wearing the proper PPE. This'

[01:03] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Close-up of the HeyGears G1X printing with blue UV light.
AUDIO: 'includes wearing gloves, a respirator, UV protective glasses because of the UV light if you\'re in here while it\'s operating, and making sure you\'re in a well-ventilated area. Stay safe, boys. Setting up the G1X was actually much easier than I expected. After unboxing'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it and plugging it in, I ran it through the initial calibration process, which only took a few minutes. You do need to fill the machine with resin, so the resin bottles are squeezed into the ports on the back of the machine. And once it\'s connected to your computer,'

[01:27] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Blueprint Studio software interface showing an image of a Pokémon card being positioned for print.
AUDIO: 'the software gives you live feedback while you\'re filling each reservoir. This really only takes a few minutes, and once all of that is done, you\'re ready to start printing. And the printing workflow is surprisingly straightforward. After placing your object on the build plate, Blueprint'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Studio takes a photo of it and measures its height automatically. From there, you simply drag and drop your artwork onto the workspace, scale it, position it, slice the file, and then hit print. Printing on cardstock paper is painless and extremely quick. I printed this'

